      "value": "茜 （akanevrc） - thank you for the detailed description and example projects. Unfortunately, I was not able to reproduce the issue on my machine. Here is what I did:\n1. Downloaded your example projects.\n2. Opened up \"UdonBeforeVCC\" and imported the sdk packages \"VRCSDK3-WORLD-2022.06.03.00.03_Public.unitypackage\" and \"UdonSharp_v0.20.3 (1).unitypackage\".\n3. Created a new UdonSharp Script and Asset named \"MomoIssueRepro\".\n4. Created three public variables on this Script, with names different than their default values like this:\n```\npublic float shouldBeTwo = 1;\npublic int shouldBeNine = 0;\npublic bool shouldBeTrue = false;\n```\n5. Added this script to a new GameObject in a new scene, and changed the variable values in the inspector to match their names like the picture on the left at the bottom of this post.\n6. Exported this GameObject, its Script and Program as a unitypackage called \"momo-issue-repro.unitypackage\".\n7. Opened the project \"UdonAfterVCC\". I had to delete the \"Packages/packages-lock.json\" file to get the git packages to properly restore.\n8. Imported the \"momo-issue-repro.unitypackage\" file into this project.\n9. Dropped the \"MomoIssueRepro\" prefab into a scene.\n10. Inspected this prefab to find that its inspector-set values were retained (picture on the right at end of post).\nAdditionally, I compared the values in the prefabs in the \"Assets/akanevrc\" folders and they appear to be the same in the \"UdonBeforeVCC\" and \"UdonAfterVCC\" projects for me.\nI'd like to help fix the issue, but I'm not sure what's happening differently on your machine and mine. Perhaps it's something we've fixed in a newer version of the SDK?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
